First line of STATUS: `GATE VERDICT B453: <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> @ <head sha7> (MPS main-red fix, test-only · C1 diff exactly the fix <y/n>, files <n>, +/- <a/b>, assertions removed or changed <n>, skip/retry/timeout added <n> · C2 widener original RED <n/n>, fixed GREEN <n/n> (TIMEOUT row), 500 row original <red/n> at 300 ms and <red/n> at 1200 ms, fixed <n/n>, restart row <n/n green>, clean-src original alone <fail/30>, fixed alone <fail/30>, own mutants t1..t4 <red/green each, as predicted y/n> · C3 product ordering can lose or delay a ticket <no/yes: which path>, restart path requeues <y/n>, findings of fact <n> · C4 class <n>x5 green <y/n>, the two rows x20 <fail/20 each>, name sets of the two filters share <n>, names lost <n> added <n> · C5 build 0/0 <y/n>, Engine/Import/Api <n/n/n>, failed <n>, skipped <n> · C6 main <not moved|moved>, merge-tree rc <n>, squash tree = head tree <y/n>, other branches touching Feedback files <n> · C7 gitleaks canary rc <n>, scan rc <n> · C8 branch CI runs <n>)`. Then: Step 0 sha256s · REFUSE counts with controls · PINS (start, mid, verdict) · instrument (dotnet version, load and slot per heavy run, every `gh` GET named) · C1-C8 each with FAIL (clock time), evidence path, result · the C2 table (condition × file × N × load1 × red/green, with the failing text of one red run quoted whole) · the C2 mutant table (mutant × anchor count × sha256 before/after × result × predicted) · findings (`B453-n`) with fix-shapes and regressions in prose · the product-risk findings of fact from C3 listed apart from the findings against the fix · FOUND / TESTED / HOW / NOT TESTED · corrections (where the builder's STATUS or this brief was wrong, with the measurement) · processes, slots, trees left · **UNMEASURED** (last section before the last line, said plainly: the CI Linux runner, the real clock behaviour of the product (a code read only), the web job, CodeQL and the GitHub CI legs, the PR, any run on a quieter machine, anything you could not